Temperature in an LLM controls randomness vs predictability in generated responses.

Think of it as:

Low temperature  → more deterministic
High temperature → more creative/random
Example

Suppose you ask:

"Suggest a startup idea"
Temperature = 0
temperature=0

Output may always be:

"AI-powered document search platform."

Very stable.
Very repeatable.

Good for:

RAG
coding
factual tasks
SQL generation
structured outputs
Temperature = 1
temperature=1

Now outputs may vary:

"AI therapist for remote workers"

"Voice-based legal assistant"

"Gamified fitness AI companion"

More creative/random.